	<item>
		<title>By: William Hageman</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=352&#038;cpage=1#comment-13476</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[William Hageman]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 14 Nov 2012 04:08:14 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=352#comment-13476</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Reading my old journals for the first time I came across an entry about David Hyams, whom I hadn&#039;t thought about for decades. I knew both he and his partner Maureeen in Vancouver around 1974-75. We did zikr together. David gave me his Turkish prayer beads before I left for Europe. A few destitute years later I wound up taking them back to where they came from, to Konya, where I studied Islam. A remarkable time in my life. His beads are still there. So sad to hear of his death. A beautiful human being.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Reading my old journals for the first time I came across an entry about David Hyams, whom I hadn&#8217;t thought about for decades. I knew both he and his partner Maureeen in Vancouver around 1974-75. We did zikr together. David gave me his Turkish prayer beads before I left for Europe. A few destitute years later I wound up taking them back to where they came from, to Konya, where I studied Islam. A remarkable time in my life. His beads are still there. So sad to hear of his death. A beautiful human being.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
		<title>By: Insu Hyams</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=352&#038;cpage=1#comment-10714</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Insu Hyams]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 01 Dec 2011 23:58:34 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=352#comment-10714</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[David had a great love for life, for his family, for kids, for God, Jesus, Sam, Hazrat Inayat Khan, and the Sufi sangha -- and for singing in Deborah&#039;s gospel choir.  He had deep appreciation for his teacher, Pir Shabda Kahn.

Dave had many struggles in his life and surmounted them all with courage, except cancer which he then used as a catapult into deeper awareness.  

He taught me lots about love.  Insu]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>David had a great love for life, for his family, for kids, for God, Jesus, Sam, Hazrat Inayat Khan, and the Sufi sangha &#8212; and for singing in Deborah&#8217;s gospel choir.  He had deep appreciation for his teacher, Pir Shabda Kahn.</p>
<p>Dave had many struggles in his life and surmounted them all with courage, except cancer which he then used as a catapult into deeper awareness.  </p>
<p>He taught me lots about love.  Insu</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
